9, 5482, 5480, 5483); Relationships (12204, 12205, 12227)].\\n\\nGlial biology is also connected to neuronal function: glial cells support neurons, astrocytes help maintain the CHEMICAL ENVIRONMENT that enables COMMUNICATION BETWEEN NERVE CELLS, and oligodendrocytes protect ELECTRICAL SIGNALING in nerve cells. By connecting tumor lineage to these support roles, the network provides a rationale for how glial-derived tumors can disrupt core neural communication systems [Data: Entities (5477, 5478, 5494, 5495, 5496); Relationships (12202, 12262, 12263, 12264)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Diagnostic workup complexity is reflected by brain tumor diagnosis context and biopsy considerations tied to tumor location\",\n      \"explanation\": \"BRAIN TUMOR DIAGNOSIS is explicitly linked to BRAIN TUMOR, framing diagnosis as a distinct, often frightening and overwhelming event and setting context for subsequent decision-making. This underscores that the community includes not only disease biology but also the patient-facing diagnostic moment as an important node [Data: Entities (4088, 4094); Relationships (8511)].\\n\\nLocation-driven diagnostic/surgical constraints appear through links from GLIOMA to HARD-TO-REACH AREA and VITAL AREA, describing how tumor placement can lead to stereotactic biopsy use or make resection difficult/unsafe and prompt biopsy planning instead. These relationships highlight that anatomic accessibility and proximity to critical structures materially influence clinical pathways [Data: Entities (5561, 5560, 5476, 4094); Relationships (12368, 12369)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 7.6,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"Impact severity is high because the community centers on malignant brain tumors—especially infiltrative gliomas with frequent treatment limitations and an explicitly stated eventual fatality for most patients—along with profound cognitive, functional, and identity-related consequences.\"\n}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, 